  concept: "Authored objective: Protect and optimize the cold chain.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the level\u2019s
    verified run history. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching
    principle: Protection logic must be verified under both normal and fault conditions,
    including reset and recovery behavior.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A safety lock must prevent unintended activation even when the normal
    switch would permit it.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Passing a normal-operation test is not proof that the protection
    system responds correctly to faults.
